   $q$Which quotation best helps explain why the speaker shovels Mrs. Abara's walk?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"I pull on my boots and my brother's old gloves\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"the sidewalk shines bare and gray.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-event"},{"text":"\"Her cane leans by the window glass.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"the snow lies smooth and deep.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Her cane leans by the window glass."$q$, $q$A cane shows that Mrs. Abara would have trouble walking on snow, so the speaker clears it for her. Deep snow is true for every house, so it does not explain why the speaker chose hers.$q$, 'draft', '3263ec3c-dacb-579a-98d8-687d2026ecd9')
